# What happens when you click a "Stage" button (or press RET on it)?
vars: {
  d2-config: {
    layout-engine: dagre
    theme-id: 0
  }
}
shape: sequence_diagram

you: You
browser: Browser
web: Browser connection plugin
kernel: Kernel
input: Input plugin

you -> browser: 1. click "Stage" on main.ss
browser -> web: 2. "activate node 42"\n(names a node, never a command)
web -> kernel: 3. put an item in the queue\n(the kernel never looks inside)
kernel -> input: 4. what does this item mean?
input -> input: 5. node 42 is still on screen, and its keymap\nbinds activate to (stage-file "main.ss")
input -> kernel: 6. run that command
kernel -> kernel: 7. runs it like any command:\nhooks, undo, C-g, macros all apply
